            <ArticleTitle>[Treatment of nociceptive pain in primary care setting].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>788-94</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The pharmacological treatment of chronic pains induced by an excess of nociception is mainly based on analgesics which are classified according to their pharmacological nature (not opioid/opioid) and to their power according to the three World Health Organization steps. Their use is founded on a strategy which differs from the nature of pain (cancer pain vs no cancer pain), in particular with regard to the use of the strong opioids.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
